 about 1.5 months, and the 5-year OS rate was about 0%, which was significantly lower than that of patients under 65 years old (45–64 years old: about 62%, <45 years old: about 80%) ( Figure 3A ). The OS rate was the lowest in patients with primary disease in other organs (such as, lung, brain, kidney, etc.) (mOS of approximately 16 months and 5-year OS rate of approximately 28%), moderate in the male reproductive system (5-year OS rate of approximately 71%), and highest in the placenta (5-year survival rate of approximately 91%) ( Figure 3B ). Table 4. Prognostic factors for patients with choriocarcinoma. Variables Univariate analysis Multivariate analysis HR (95% CI) P HR (95% CI) P Age (years) <45 Reference Reference 45–64 1.886 (1.246–2.856) 0.003 1.940 (1.225–3.072) 0.005 ≥65 13.695 (8.192–22.892) <0.001 5.504 (3.093–9.793) <0.001 Sex Female Reference Reference Male 2.576 (1.787–3.713) <0.001 0.771 (0.369–1.610) 0.49 Race Black Reference White 0.654 (0.411–1.041) 0.07 Other 0.674 (0.368–1.235) 0.20 Marital Married Reference Reference Other 1.573 (1.115–2.218) 0.009 1.500 (1.035–2.174) 0.03 pSite Female Rep Reference Reference Male Rep 1.816 (1.049–3.143) 0.03 2.511 (1.027–6.141) 0.04 Placenta 0.425 (0.195–0.924) 0.03 0.350 (0.158–0.778) 0.01 Other 7.792 (4.332–14.015) <0.001 4.567 (2.062–10.118) <0.001 Histologic type 9100 Reference Reference 9101 0.634 (0.448–0.898) 0.01 0.668 (0.442–1.009) 0.055 Lung metastasis No/unknown Reference Reference Yes 2.784 (2.005–3.866) <0.001 1.720 (1.125–2.629) 0.01 Liver metastasis No/unknown Reference Reference Yes 4.084 (2.913–5.725) <0.001 1.764 (1.214–2.564) 0.003 Bone metastasis No/unknown Reference Reference Yes 2.889 (1.472–5.667) 0.002 0.739 (0.352–1.552) 0.43 Brain metastasis No/unknown Reference Reference Yes 3.880 (2.728–5.518) <0.001 1.515 (0.964–2.382) 0.07 Surgery No Reference Reference Yes 0.418 (0.305–0.573) <0.001 0.504 (0.344–0.738) <0.001 Radiation No/unknown Reference Reference Yes 3.864 (2.614–5.712) <0.001